  exitDialoguesPassed:
    lastVerdict: 1
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - Cool. Have a fun time in your little box, officer.
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - "Right. I\u2019m going to go stare at a wall now."
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - Whatever. See you when the lights go out for good.
  exitDialoguesQuarantined:
    lastVerdict: 2
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - A holding cell? Does it have a bed? I could use a nap.
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - Fine. At least I don't have to tell people we're out of sugar in there.
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - "Put me wherever. It\u2019s all the same to me at this point."
  exitDialoguesKilled:
    lastVerdict: 3
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - Oh. I guess... I don't have to... go to work... tomorrow...
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - This is... a very... loud way... to end a shift...
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - Finally... I can... stop... waiting... in lines.
  quarantineExitLines:
  - Okay.
  - Does it have a chair? Great. Fine.
  - "Sure. Lock me up. I\u2019ll add it to the list of things that don\u2019t matter."
  killExitLines:
  - "Hm. Didn\u2019t even need to think about it, did you."
  - "Right. Okay. That\u2019s\u2026 fine too\u2026 I guess\u2026"
  - "At least I don\u2019t\u2026 have to face another line\u2026 tomorrow\u2026"
