  introDialogue: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 99e1cc7b15baa0d419ddc8e8574252f3, type: 2}
  questionResponses:
  - question: Where are you coming from?
    earlyDaysAnswer: The shop. I was closing up.
    midDaysAnswer: The shop. We ran out of almost everything again.
    finalDaysAnswer: I don't really remember. Somewhere gray.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: Home. I haven't been in for days. There's nothing left
      to sell anyway.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: Home. Haven't been to the shop in a while. The shelves
      are empty. No point.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: The shop. Still open. Still stocked. Everything is fine.
      Completely fine.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
  - question: Have you been experiencing any strange symptoms lately?
    earlyDaysAnswer: No. I'm fine. I'm always fine.
    midDaysAnswer: I've been tired. More than usual. I don't know if that counts.
    finalDaysAnswer: Everything kind of aches. But I think that's how it is now.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: Yes, actually. I'm exhausted. Haven't felt fine in weeks.
      I don't know why I said fine.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: No tiredness. I feel the same as I always do. Normal.
      Which is fine.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: Nothing aches. I'm fine. I've always been fine. I'll
      be fine.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
  - question: Who do you live with?
    earlyDaysAnswer: I live alone. It's quieter that way.
    midDaysAnswer: Alone. My neighbor stopped responding about two weeks ago.
    finalDaysAnswer: Just me. Which is fine.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: My wife. She moved in last month. It's noisier now.
      I don't mind.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: My neighbor and I spoke this morning. He is fine. We are
      both fine.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: My wife. She moved in recently. She's there when I get
      home. I'm fairly sure.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
  idleBarks:
    earlyDays:
    - Is your stamp working? Ours at the shop broke twice this week.
    - There was no bread again. I stood in line for an hour anyway. Force of habit.
    - You look like you are about to ask me something. Please do not.
    - Take your time. I have nothing urgent waiting for me on the other side.
    midDays:
    - The shop is empty. I still open it every morning. I am not sure why.
    - Are you cold? I stopped feeling cold about a week ago. Not sure what that means.
    - Someone was crying in the street on the way here. I walked past. There was
      nothing to do.
    finalDays:
    - Does any of this feel pointless to you? Just curious. I will not be offended.
    - I keep coming through here. Pure habit at this point. Take your time.
    - I have nowhere to be. Neither does anyone.
    uncannyEarlyDays: []
    uncannyMidDays: []
    uncannyFinalDays: []
